Greetings!

After not playing nethack for about 1 year I started again around
christmas.  Steadily improving my games I got very lucky with my
latest game, a lawful human valkyrie.

I found several useful tools (pick-axe, magic whistle) early on and
got a co-aligned temple in Minetown.  Got Excalibur by #dipping.  Then
I found a wand of wishing in Sokoban.  With that I got gray dragon
scale mail, an amulet of reflection (the sokoban reward was a bag of
holding) and an oilskin cloak.  Later I found gauntlets of power, a
Hawaiian shirt and got speed boots through a wish from a throne.

After that I finished the quest which was easy as usual with
valkyries.  Found Fort Ludios and got 2 wands of death from the
soldiers there.  With the gold I bought protection in Minetown and
descended towards the Castle.  Lacking a source of levitation I dug
down from Medusa's Island and and climbed back up to kill her.  Still
I had no luck with the statue of Perseus, it only contained a bag.
Descending a bit further I found levitation boots and a helm of
opposite alignment.  Alas, I completely forgot about the existence of
this item (well, it really was a long time since I played regularly)
and lost my protection.  This was no real problem though, as I had
holy water and there was more than enough gold left at Fort Ludios.
After buying protection for a second time I accidently attacked the
priest (I still don't know how, must have been real life gauntlets of
fumbling) and escaped Minetown as my business there was finished
anyway.

I found another co-aligned altar in the dungeon on the way down again
towards the Castle.  Arriving at the Castle I solved the passtune
riddle and cleared the first room with the help of the drawbridge.
After clearing the rest of the Castle "by hand" I used the wand of
wishing for 2 blessed scrolls of genocide, two magic markers (there
were none to be found in the dungeon) and Frost Brand.  Enchanted my
armor and Frost Brand as well as a silver saber and 7 daggers and
genocided L, h and R.  Saving the wand of wishing with one charge I
descended into the Valley of the Dead.

Dug my way through the mazes of Gehennom and paid of Asmodeus with a
heap of gold found on the same level.  Further down I met Juiblex
which was easily finished with a wand of digging while engulfed.  I
can't really remember Baalzebub so he can't have been that tough.
Orcus was also easy and yielded yet another wand of death.

Further down I killed Vlad and marked the Vibrating Square.  Having
met Rodney only in two games before which both ended deadly I got a
bit nervous and postponed meeting him.  I found a helm of telepathy
somewhere along the way and got Mjollnir through a sacrifice.  Still I
put it in a stash in Sokoban as I wanted to keep Frost Brand.  Still
not feeling really prepared, I reverse genocided nurses in Sokoban and
increased my max HP to about 200.  To somewhat complete my ascension
kit I used the wand of wishing then for a ring of levitation and one
of free action (wresting a last charge out of the wand).

Now I felt that I had to ascend or die trying and dumped everything I
could no longer use and packed some more food.  Now I was to meet
Rodney.  Some monster summoned Yeenoghu in the zoo but he was easily
finished with my highly enchanted weapons.  Killed Rodney with my wand
of death and retrieved the Book of the Dead from his moat with a wand
of cold.  I went down to perform the invocation ritual.  Dropping the
Book I descended into Moloch's Sanctum.  In my best earlier game I
died here so I proceeded carefully.  Clearing the graveyard and the
surroundings of the temple was no real problem though.  Wasted all
charges of the Bell of Opening trying to find the entrance but had to
do it manually in the end.  The priest got killed by one of my wands
of death and I retrieved the Amulet of Yendor.  Seeing that the way
back was relatively clear I decided to save my cursed potion of gain
level and started ascending.  Got pulled back three levels annoyingly
often but arrived in the Valley of the Dead without meeting Rodney
again.  I met him once more on my way up but I still had more than
enough charges in my wands of death.  On level 1 I took a deep breath,
checked my kit and the Amulet and climbed.

The Plane of Earth was easy as I had several wands of digging.  The
Wizard of Yendor once again got a blast from my wand of death (he
simply doesn't learn) and I used up all charges of my Orb of Fate to
find the portal.  Putting on my ring of levitation I arrived on the
Plane of Air which was also not that tough.  Got engulfed by air
elementals several times which was the most dangerous situation on the
elemental planes.  Still I survived and saw a monster use the portal.
Arriving on the Plane of Fire I went around in circles followed by a
horde of monsters but stepped accidently on the portal myself.  The
Plane of Water was easy but annoying.  I used my one scroll of gold
detection while confused but was too slow to catch the bubble with the
portal.  Also stepped accidently on it later as it was hidden under a
corpse.

The middle temple on the Astral Plane had Famine, so I decided to try
this one first.  Famine died after two attacks of mine and the rest of
the monsters where no real problem.  Still the altar in the middle was
neutral, so not even a chance with my helm of opposite alignment.  Not
really wanting to fight Pestilence as I was seriously lacking in full
healing potions I went to the left temple and got attacked by Death.
As I had more than 200 HP at this point, his attacks were not that
dangerous and I killed him fast.  Arriving at the temple I found that
it was Tyr (lawful) and I offered the Amulet of Yendor to Tyr...
An invisible choir sang, and I was bathed in radiance...
The voice of Tyr boomed out: "Congratulations, mortal!"
"In return to thy service, I grant thee the gift of Immortality!"
Now I, too, am a Demigod(ess). Phew.

Looking back my preparations were perhaps a bit excessive, especially
the hit points.  I would have needed less food, too, as I had a ring
of slow digestion.  There were also many charges left in my wands of
death, I should perhaps have made more use of those.  Now I'll try to
ascend a wizard for a change.

